# org-terms.conf — what check-core-clean.sh scans for.
#
# Copy to `scripts/org-terms.conf` and fill in your organization's real terms.
# That file is gitignored: naming the organization in a committed file would
# leak it the moment the repository is published, which is the exact thing this
# check exists to prevent. Keep the filled copy private — in the overlay plugin,
# in a password manager, or simply untracked.
#
# Format, one rule per line:
#
#   <id>|<BLOCK|WARN>|<description>|<extended regex>
#
#   BLOCK  never publishable — it belongs in the overlay plugin
#   WARN   a judgement call — confirm it is genuinely generic before publishing
#
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. The regex is passed to
# `grep -E`, so escape dots you mean literally and use `|` inside a group, never
# at the top level of the pattern (the top-level `|` separates the fields).

# --- identity -----------------------------------------------------------------

org-name|BLOCK|organization named|(ExampleCorp|example\.com)
corp-email|BLOCK|corporate email address|[a-zA-Z0-9._%+-]+@example\.com

# --- internal systems ---------------------------------------------------------
# Identifiers whose access is gated by an ACL are still infrastructure detail:
# they name what exists and where, which is not yours to publish.

confluence|BLOCK|Confluence space or page id|(CONFLUENCE_[A-Z_]+[[:space:]]*=|spaceId[[:space:]]*[0-9]{6,})
drive|BLOCK|Google Drive file or folder id|drive\.google\.com/(drive/folders|file/d)/[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}
jira|BLOCK|internal Jira project key|\b(PROJ|DSP)-[0-9]{3,}\b
internal-host|BLOCK|internal hostname|[a-z0-9-]+\.(internal|corp|intranet)\b

# --- brand and design ---------------------------------------------------------

design-system|WARN|named design system|(ExampleCorp Design System|\bXDS\b)
ds-ids|WARN|bare design-system component id|data-[a-z]+-page="[0-9]{9,}"

# --- posture ------------------------------------------------------------------
# A regulatory stance describes the organization, not the tool. Generic advice
# about handling personal data is fine in core; "we are a regulated operator
# under X" is not.

regulatory|WARN|org regulatory posture|(\bDORA\b|EU AI Act|regulated (financial )?operator)
